{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788971468,"nonce":"NcRci5kKMcak9lvSdcmcuhApGyo=","title":"decisions panel counts an ordinary letter's Close/Jump buttons as a choice","message":"Every standard letter becomes an owed decision, so `decisions` fills with noise and a real choice will be buried in it. Found on day 1 of openrun-20260909.\n\n## What happened\n\nTwo Nepo shipment-arrival letters produced two owed decisions:\n\n    \"id\": \"d-letter-0\", \"kind\": \"letter\", \"def\": \"PositiveEvent\", \"type\": \"StandardLetter\",\n    \"text\": \"Shipment arrived — a letter with a choice. It waits, and it will keep waiting.\",\n    \"acts\": [ letter-choose {letter:0, option:0} \"Close\",\n               letter-choose {letter:0, option:1} \"Jump to location\",\n               letter-read   {letter:0} ]\n\n`total_owed: 2`, `by_kind: {\"letter\": 2}`.\n\nNeither is a choice. **Close** dismisses the letter and **Jump to location** moves the camera — every letter with a `lookTargets` has both, and `type` is `StandardLetter`, not `ChoiceLetter`. `options_disabled: 0` is consistent with there being no real options to disable.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n- The run contract's rule 6 is \"never advance past a letter that carries a CHOICE — not past a bad letter, past a choice\". A panel that calls every letter a choice makes that rule unreadable: on this colony the two entries were a delivery I placed myself.\n- `decisions.gate` says the answer gate is 975973e's second half and NOT ENFORCED. **When it lands, these would block advances** — an unanswerable obligation generated by the colony's own supply run.\n- The contract already grades the agent on \"every decision you were asked and what you answered\". Noise here inflates that count with nothing.\n\n## The discriminator\n\n`RimWorld/ChoiceLetter` and its subclasses are the letters that carry options; `StandardLetter` is the plain one. `ChoiceLetter.Choices` is the real option set, and its base `Option_Close` / the `lookTargets` jump are the two that every letter has. Suggested rule: a letter is a decision when it is a `ChoiceLetter` with at least one option that is neither the close option nor the jump — check against `ChoiceLetter.Option_Close` and the camera-jump option rather than counting buttons.\n\nWorth checking the same question for `Letter.CanShowInLetterStack` and for quest letters, which are the case that must NOT be lost.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A Nepo shipment letter, a research-complete letter and any other `StandardLetter` produce **no** owed decision; `total_owed` stays 0 through a delivery.\n- A genuine `ChoiceLetter` — a joiner/wanderer offer, a quest offer, a trade caravan, a refugee — DOES produce one, with its real options in `acts` and the close/jump buttons not presented as the choice.\n- The distinguishing test is stated in the panel's own `set`/basis line so a reader can tell what was counted.\n- Regression guard for the contract's rule 6: the letter that offers a free colonist must appear in `decisions`; the letter that says a pod landed must not.","files":null}]}